{"answer_type":"grounded_answer","answer":"Three assumptions in current approaches for defining faithfulness are:

1. The Model Assumption: Two models will make the same predictions if and only if they use the same reasoning process. (cited in E2, E4, E6)
2. The Prediction Assumption: On similar inputs, the model makes similar decisions if and only if its reasoning is similar. (cited in E5)
3. The Decision Assumption: An interpretation is unfaithful if it results in different decisions than the model it interprets. (cited in E6)

